Here is a Python solution for the problem. The function `rec` takes an array as input and returns the maximum length of a sorted array that can be obtained using Thanos sort. The function checks if the array is already sorted and returns its length if it is. If not, it calculates the middle index of the array and recursively calls itself on the two halves of the array. The maximum length of the sorted array is the maximum of the lengths of the sorted arrays obtained from the two halves.

